# What never enters a build context.
#
# This file is a security control before it is an optimisation. Everything listed here
# would otherwise be sent to the daemon and be reachable by any `COPY .`, and a secret that
# reaches a layer stays in that layer even if a later instruction deletes it - `docker
# history` and any registry pull can read it back. So the rule is not "do not COPY .env",
# which is a rule somebody has to remember; it is "`.env` cannot be in the context", which
# is a rule the tool enforces.

# --- Credentials. The reason this file exists. -----------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Derived data, and the two directories that dominate the context by size -----------
# `data/vector_store/` is a built Chroma index and `data/raw|processed/` are downloads and
# parquet. None of the three is copied into an image by decision (ADR-0010): the index is
# mounted, the model comes from the registry at runtime. Excluding them here means a build
# does not even transfer them.
data/
mlruns/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Tooling caches, notebooks and history ---------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
notebooks/
docs/
tests/
*.ipynb
.pre-commit-config.yaml
Taskfile.yml
